      "title": "Position Description: Vice President of Institutional Advancement",
      "description": "Vice President of Institutional Advancement - Hartsville, SC - Coker University Jobs Jobs | Login Location: Hartsville, SC, USA Pay Rate: $150000 - $180000 per year Pay Type: per year Employment Type: Full Time Email Me This Job Position Description: Vice President of Institutional Advancement Position Summary The Vice President of Institutional Advancement drives transformative philanthropic support and fosters a culture of excellence, integrity, and high performance at Coker University. Reporting directly to the President, the Vice President serves as a key, highly collaborative member of the Executive Leadership Team (ELT) to align advancement priorities with the university's strategic mission. This leader will play a pivotal role in driving the execution and success of Coker's upcoming major fundraising campaign. Operating with a growth mindset while building advancement staff, the Vice President utilizes a business development approach to cultivate, steward, and move individual and organizational prospects through a strategic investment pipeline. This position establishes and monitors clear performance goals, metrics, and accountability frameworks for both the division and themselves. The role focuses on securing financial funding while simultaneously leveraging external resources and elevating lifelong alumni engagement across the Coker community while understanding the role of relationships in a rural community. Key Responsibilities Executive Leadership & Campaign Execution Serve as a key collaborative partner on the Coker University Executive Leadership Team. Report directly to the President, providing strategic counsel on institutional advancement. Serve as a central driver and key leader in executing the university's upcoming fundraising campaign. Work closely with the President and fellow executives to align advancement with strategic campus goals. Bridge the advancement division with other campus areas to maximize collective expertise. Philanthropic Leadership & Strategy Provide strategic direction for all university fundraising and philanthropic endeavors. Inspire a lasting culture of generosity among alumni, Cobras, donors, and stakeholders. Share impactful stories of how a Coker education changes lives to inspire prospective funders. Business Development & Pipeline Management Move prospects efficiently through the university's institutional investment pipeline. Build, monitor, and enforce divisional goals, metrics, and accountability. Maximize both financial investments and alternative resource cultivation. Relationship Building & Stewardship Cultivate meaningful relationships with alumni, regional donors, and community partners. Foster long-term trust, connection, and loyalty to Coker University. Practice empathetic, active listening to establish deep rapport with stakeholders. Alumni Engagement Innovation Design innovative strategies to maximize global Coker alumni involvement. Leverage modern technology, targeted events, and distinct programming. Build strong, diverse, and lifelong connections within the alumni network. Performance Leadership Lead, mentor, and develop a high-performing team of advancement professionals. Cultivate an internal team culture of excellence, collaboration, and continuous improvement. Champion a culture of strict integrity, professional ethics, and responsible resource stewardship. Position Requirements Education & Experience Minimum Bachelor's Degree from an accredited institution. Minimum seven years of relevant experience in business development within higher education or related corporate industries. Demonstrated track record of playing a key role in executing major capital or fundraising campaigns. Experience establishing and tracking quantitative divisional performance metrics. Key Competencies Executive Collaboration: Ability to work cohesively within an executive leadership framework to solve complex institutional challenges. Campaign Driving: Proven ability to mobilize resources and hit milestones during large-scale institutional campaigns. Growth Mindset: Continuously seeks innovative ways to expand institutional reach and resources. Relationship Building: Easily establishes rapport and deep trust with diverse stakeholders. Communication: Exceptional active listening skills paired with inspiring storytelling abilities. Accountability: Strong focus on metrics, data-driven decisions, and performance tracking. Coker University https://coker.isolvedhire.com Apply Now You have JavaScript disabled on your browser. You will not be able to apply for this position without enabling javascript. If you need assistance with enabling javascript, please click here for assistance. * Fields Are Required About You: First Name Initial Last Name Contact Info: Email Confirm Email Phone Number Number Type Home Cell Work Preferred Method of Contact: Email Text Message Address: Street Address Line 1 Street Address Line 2 Country/Territory Country/Territory* United States Canada Australia New Zealand United Kingdom Afghanistan Aland Islands Albania Algeria American Samoa Andorra Angola Anguilla Antarctica Antigua and Barbuda Argentina Armenia Aruba Asia/Pacific Region Austria Azerbaijan Bahamas Bahrain Bangladesh Barbados Belarus Belgium Belize Benin Bermuda Bhutan Bolivia Bosnia and Herzegovina Botswana Bouvet Island Brazil British Indian Ocean Territory Brunei Darussalam Bulgaria Burkina Faso Burundi Cambodia Cameroon Cape Verde Caribbean Cayman Islands Central African Republic Chad Chile China Christmas Island Cocos (Keeling) Islands Colombia Comoros Congo Congo  The Democratic Republic of the Cook Islands Costa Rica Cote d'Ivoire Croatia Cuba Cyprus Czech Republic Denmark Djibouti Dominica Dominican Republic Ecuador Egypt El Salvador Equatorial Guinea Eritrea Estonia Ethiopia Europe Falkland Islands (Malvinas) Faroe Islands Fiji Finland France France  Metropolitan French Guiana French Polynesia French Southern Territories Gabon Gamb