      "description": "Assistant or Associate Professor of Physical Education - Hartsville, SC - Coker University Jobs Jobs | Login Location: Hartsville, SC, USA Pay Rate: Pay Type: Employment Type: Full Time Email Me This Job College of Health Professions | Physical Education and Sport Studies Program Position Title: Full-Time, Tenure-Track Assistant or Associate Professor of Physical Education and Sport Studies • Appointment Type: 9-Month Full-Time, Tenure-Track • Start Date: August 2027 • Reporting Structure: Reports directly to the Dean of the College of Health Professions • Compensation: Competitive salary and comprehensive benefits package Position Overview & Purpose The Coker University Physical Education and Sport Studies Program invites applications for a full-time, tenure-track Assistant or Associate Professor in Physical Education ( Kinesiology, Exercise Science, Exercise Physiology) beginning August 2027. Primary responsibilities center on high-quality, inclusive in-person teaching alongside selective online course delivery. Coker University seeks an educator who is passionate about teaching, applies inclusive pedagogy, and is dedicated to working with students in classroom and laboratory-based settings. The ideal candidate desires to develop meaningful, collegial working relationships across campus, is eager to contribute interests and ideas for new and innovative courses and programming, and is committed to actively contributing to Coker's mission. Coker University is committed to proactively mentoring new faculty members, supporting a robust culture of undergraduate research, and utilizing diverse pedagogical approaches that promote student persistence and success. Key Responsibilities ● Instruction & Pedagogy: Teach 12 credit hours per semester (24 credit hours per academic year) across undergraduate coursework in Exercise Science (Kinesiology, Exercise Physiology, Measurement and Evaluation), foundational program courses (Introduction to Physical Education), and Health/Fitness courses (Fitness Appraisal, First Aid/CPR, Lifetime Fitness, Personal and Community Health) as needed. Utilize inclusive pedagogy in both face-to-face and selective online environments. ● Innovative Program & Curriculum Development: Eagerly contribute interests and ideas to design, implement, and recruit students for new and innovative courses and academic programming. Participate in ongoing curriculum evaluation and collect and analyze data required for ● AHA BLS Leadership: Serve as, or demonstrate a willingness to become certified as, an American Heart Association (AHA) Basic Life Support (BLS) Instructor to support departmental First Aid/CPR and health/fitness course delivery and student certification needs. ● Student Advising & Success: Assist in advising and mentoring Physical Education majors, support students in navigating the university's Learning Management System (Brightspace), and apply best practices to student success and retention initiatives. ● Student Recruitment: Actively recruit Physical Education majors through individual and group meetings with prospective students and parents during admissions events, open houses, and student orientation programming. ● University & Professional Service: Serve on program, standing university, task force, and Faculty Senate committees. Participate in community and professional activities as appropriate. ● Scholarly Activity & Collaboration: Participate in scholarly projects and collaborate effectively with faculty and staff within Physical Education and across the university to develop inter-professional academic and research opportunities. Qualifications Required Qualifications: ● Earned Doctorate (Ph.D. or Ed.D.) in Exercise Science, Kinesiology, Exercise Physiology, or a closely related field. ● Successful university-level teaching experience in Exercise Science and related fields, primarily in face-to-face classroom and laboratory settings. ● Demonstrated interest and enthusiasm for creating, developing, and expanding new and innovative academic programming and course offerings. Preferred Attributes: ● Teaching or Research Expertise in Sport Psychology: Demonstrated background, academic focus, or teaching experience in Sport Psychology or Exercise Psychology. ● Inclusive Pedagogy: Demonstrated passion for teaching and evidence of implementing inclusive pedagogical strategies. ● Undergraduate Mentorship: Strong commitment to working closely with undergraduate students in classroom, laboratory, and student research environments. ● Collegial Collaboration: Collaborative leadership style with a desire to build strong, collegial working relationships across campus. ● Mission Alignment: Alignment with Coker's mission to support undergraduate research, proactive faculty mentorship, and student academic success. Application Instructions Review of application materials will begin immediately and will continue until the position is filled. Interested candidates must submit application materials online at https://coker.isolvedhire.com/pages/JobOpportunities. A complete application packet must include: ● Cover Letter (addressing qualifications, teaching experience, interest in program innovation, and vision for the role) ● Curriculum Vitae (CV) ● Statement of Teaching Philosophy ● Statement describing how you have promoted student belonging and inclusion ● Copies of Transcripts (official transcripts required upon hire) ● Complete contact information for three (3) professional references About Coker University Located in Hartsville, South Carolina, and founded in 1908, Coker University is a student-centered university granting bachelor's degrees in 30+ subject areas (including five degrees earned entirely online) and three master's degrees earned entirely online. Coker is consistently ranked among the 'Best Regional Universities in the South' by U.S. News & World Report and 'Best Southeastern Schools' by The Princeton Review. More information is available at coker.edu and cokercobras.com. Equal Opportunity Statement Coker University, in compliance with all applicable state and federal laws, including Titles VI and VII of the Civil Rights Act of 1964, Title IX of the Education Amendments of 1972, Section 504 of the Rehabilitation Act of 1973, and the Americans with Disabilities Act of 1990, does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, ethnicity, national origin, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity and expression, age, marital status, veterans or military status, or against individuals with disabilities, or other legally protected classifications in the areas of employment, admission, financial aid or access to educational or extracurricular programs, activities or facilities. University Standard Service and Excellence Expectations Coker's standards of service and excellence to the campus and community is an institutional priority for the university. We pride ourselves in our customer service, communication, and availability to our stakeholders and employees through efficient response times, detailed information, and professionalism. Being part of Coker University means committing to our Culture of COBRAS. We believe in showing up for students and colleagues with care, openness, bold ideas, and a drive to be remarkable and adaptable-always striking at the opportunity to be better. Coker University readies undergraduates for personal and professional success through a distinctive four-year program that emphasizes a practical application of the liberal arts as well as hands-on and discussion-based learning within and beyond the classroom. Located in Hartsville, SC, Coker is within two hours of the cultural, financial and recreational resources of Charlotte, Columbia, Charleston and Myrtle Beach. Coker University, in compliance with all applicable state and federal laws, including Titles VI and VII of the Civil Rights Act of 1964, Title IX of the Education Amendments of 1972, Section 504 of the Rehabilitation Act of 1973, and the Americans with Disabilities Act of 1990, does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, ethnicity, national origin, ancestry, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity and expression, age, marital status, veterans or military status, or against individuals with disabilities, medical condition, or other legally protected classifications in the areas of employment, admission, financial aid or access to educational or extracurricular programs, activities or facilities. Coker University https://coker.isolvedhire.com Apply Now You have JavaScript disabled on your browser. You will not be able to apply for this position without enabling javascript. If you need assistance with enabling javascript, please click here for assistance. * Fields Are Required About You: First Name Initial Last Name Contact Info: Email Confirm Email Phone Number Number Type Home Cell Work Preferred Method of Contact: Email Text Message Address: Street Address Line 1 Street Address Line 2 Country/Territory Country/Territory* United States Canada Australia New Zealand United Kingdom Afghanistan Aland Islands Albania Algeria American Samoa Andorra Angola Anguilla Antarctica Antigua and Barbuda Argentina Armenia Aruba Asia/Pacific Region Austria Azerbaijan Bahamas Bahrain Bangladesh Barbados Belarus Belgium Belize Benin Bermuda Bhutan Bolivia Bosnia and Herzegovina Botswana Bouvet Island Brazil British Indian Ocean Territory Brunei Darussalam Bulgaria Burkina Faso Burundi Cambodia Cameroon Cape Verde Caribbean Cayman Islands Central African Republic Chad Chile China Christmas Island Cocos (Keeling) Islands Colombia Comoros Congo Congo  The Democratic Republic of the Cook Islands Costa Rica Cote d'Ivoire Croatia Cuba Cyprus Czech Republic Denmark Djibouti Dominica Dominican Republic Ecuador Egypt El Salvador Equatorial Guinea Eritrea Estonia Ethiopia Europe Falkland Islands (Malvinas) Faroe Islands Fiji Finland France France  Metropolitan French Guiana French